&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TripleLift delivers measurable outcomes through orchestration of creative, supply, audience, and intelligence. To turn that strategy into results, we are seeking a Chief of Staff to serve as a strategic thought partner to the CEO and a force multiplier for the executive team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Chief of Staff plays a critical role in how TripleLift shapes, executes, and communicates its most important strategic initiatives. In this position, you will partner closely with the CEO, executive leadership, and our private equity sponsor to pressure-test plans, drive cross-functional execution, and keep priorities from being diluted as they move through the organization. This is not an administrative role. It is an opportunity for someone who wants to help create and execute strategy, and who is comfortable moving between high-level thinking and hands-on work. The role is a stepping stone to a senior strategy, operations or P&amp;amp;L leadership position. This is a hybrid position based in our New York City office, with an expectation of working in the office three days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a thought partner to the CEO and executive team on strategic questions, building and interpreting the KPIs that tie directly to the company’s strategic mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sit on the exec team as a direct report to the CEO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help create and drive cross-functional strategic initiatives across finance, operations, and go-to-market, including margin improvement, cost takeout, growth programs, and transformation work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pressure-test plans for feasibility before rollout and give candid, data-backed feedback to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run or support 100-day plans, synergy tracking, and carve-out or integration workstreams for mergers and acquisitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate strategy and outcomes to varied audiences, including employees, the board of directors, and financial sponsors, and prepare board and sponsor materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the CEO’s executive operating rhythm, including reporting cadences, executive team and board preparation, follow-through on commitments, and cross-functional coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted liaison between the C-suite and the broader organization, influencing without authority to keep initiatives on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or post-undergraduate master’s degree is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 4 years of experience at a top strategy consulting firm, ideally with exposure to corporate strategy, operations, or private equity portfolio work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience working inside private equity portfolio companies (as an embedded resource, EIR, or through a PE operating group) on margin improvement, driving operating leverage, or growth initiatives is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running or supporting 100-day plans, M&amp;amp;A, synergy tracking, or carve-out and integration workstreams, ideally across tech, finance, operations, and go-to-market functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort moving between high-level strategy and day-to-day execution, reporting cadences, and cross-functional coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discreet, low-ego, high-output, with strong relationship skills and the ability to act as a force multiplier for a CEO and executive team without needing the spotlight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Military background is a plus: former operational commissioned officer (Army, Navy, Marine Corps, or Air Force), ideally with experience leading teams under operational pressure and tight timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Jobs:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;The base salary range represents the low and high end of the TripleLift US salary range for this position. Actual salaries will vary depending on factors including but not limited to experience and performance. The range listed is just one component of TripleLift’s total compensation package for employees. Other rewards may include bonuses, an open Paid Time Off policy, and many region-specific benefits.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;Pay is based on various non-discriminatory factors including but not limited to experience, education, and skills.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;Benefits Available to Eligible Employees Include the following*:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &#39;Segoe UI&#39;, Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, &#39;Open Sans&#39;, &#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Medical, Dental &amp;amp; Vision Plans&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &#39;Segoe UI&#39;, Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, &#39;Open Sans&#39;, &#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Flexible PTO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;401k w/ employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Full-time employees are eligible for comprehensive benefits (subject to the terms of applicable plans/policies/agreements, which will be made available to you after commencing employment).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary range transparency&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$250,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At TripleLift, we believe great work starts with great people. We foster a culture built on collaboration, curiosity, and a shared commitment to making each other better. We move with urgency, challenge convention, and continuously innovate to elevate digital advertising. We value people who bring new perspectives, take ownership, and work together to drive meaningful impact. Learn more about TripleLift and our culture on our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/triplelift/life/tripleliftpeopleculturecommunity&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn Life page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://triplelift.com/privacy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for information about how TripleLift handles personal information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;TripleLift does not accept unsolicited resumes from recruitment search firms. Any resume submitted without a signed agreement in place will become the property of TripleLift, and no fee will be due.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
